WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:00.667
New this morning, we have

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:02.102
some reporting out of Washington, D.C.

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:02.902
The Justice Department

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:03.770
wants answers

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.805
about a confusing chain of events

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:06.873
that delayed the discovery

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:09.843
of a box of classified documents at Mar

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:10.577
a Lago.

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:11.111
Sources say

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:13.113
the contents were copied,

00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:15.281
emailed, moved to an offsite location

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:17.250
before returning to the former

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.351
president's office.

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:19.519
Former President Trump, I'm

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:20.720
talking about exactly where

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.456
the FBI had searched just weeks earlier.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.091
Explanation for all of this now.

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:26.359
CNN's Paula Reid

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:27.861
live on Capitol Hill with more.

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:28.795
Good morning to you.

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:29.729
So what is this

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:31.831
what what's going on here?

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:32.565
Well, Don,

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:33.266
the special counsel

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:33.900
investigators,

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:34.834
they want to know why

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:35.969
classified documents

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:37.470
keep showing up at Mar

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.406
a Lago as recently as December

00:00:39.406 --> 00:00:40.907
that's nearly two years

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:42.942
after Trump left office.

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:44.010
And the big question

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.045
for the special counsel

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:45.912
is whether this is just

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:47.914
the result of carelessness

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:48.882
or if this is part

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:50.350
of some sort of intentional effort

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:52.419
to obstruct their investigation.

00:00:52.419 --> 00:00:52.786
We've learned

00:00:52.786 --> 00:00:53.620
from our reporting

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:54.454
that they were specifically

00:00:54.454 --> 00:00:55.488
interested in a box

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:56.856
that was uncovered by Trump

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:58.591
lawyers in December.

00:00:58.591 --> 00:00:59.759
This box contained

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:00.860
what was described to us

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:03.763
as a handful of classified documents.

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:05.331
But complicating matters

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:07.667
is the fact that back in 20, 21,

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.469
a young staffer was instructed

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:12.872
to scan the contents of this box,

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.174
just scan it with her phone

00:01:14.174 --> 00:01:16.142
and put those documents on a laptop.

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:17.877
Now, we've learned that after

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:18.578
she scanned them,

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:19.412
this box was sent

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:21.548
to an offsite storage space

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:23.316
and only recently returned to Mar

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:24.117
a Lago,

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:25.852
where it was uncovered in December

00:01:25.852 --> 00:01:27.320
in a momento closet

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:28.354
where the former president

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:30.690
keeps challenge coins and other mementos.

00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:32.192
Now, federal investigators

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:33.626
now have the laptop.

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:35.328
They have the box of documents,

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:36.696
they have a thumb drive.

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:38.131
And we've learned that in recent weeks.

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:40.166
They also sat down with a staffer

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.135
to ask what exactly happened here?

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:43.670
How did she come into possession

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:45.405
of these classified documents?

00:01:45.405 --> 00:01:46.973
Because they want to know why

00:01:46.973 --> 00:01:48.675
this box was not given

00:01:48.675 --> 00:01:49.909
to the Justice Department,

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:51.811
how it conveniently eluded

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:53.980
a federal searches of that property

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:55.315
and whether the former president

00:01:55.315 --> 00:01:56.249
had any knowledge

00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:58.218
or anything to do with this.

00:01:58.218 --> 00:02:00.420
There's a really interesting development,

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:01.154
and that is,

00:02:01.154 --> 00:02:01.454
you know,

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:02.989
renowned conservative judge

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:03.690
Michael Luttig

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:05.492
is slamming Mike Pence

00:02:05.492 --> 00:02:08.161
for not only defying the special counsel

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:09.028
Jack Smith subpoena,

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:11.464
but also calling it unconstitutional

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:13.166
and unprecedented.

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:13.933
Well, how can you

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:14.767
how significant

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:16.936
is that to hear that from Luttig?

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:17.971
This is so interesting,

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:19.072
Poppy, because, of course,

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:20.974
this judge is a long time Pence ally.

00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:22.275
This is someone who helped him

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:24.010
work through the certification

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:25.478
of the electoral results,

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:27.714
called him a hero of democracy.

00:02:27.914 --> 00:02:29.582
So now the fact that he's coming out

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:30.183
and he says, look,

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:31.985
Pence doesn't have a chance in the world

00:02:31.985 --> 00:02:33.386
of defeating this subpoena

00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:34.487
from the special counsel.

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:35.688
This is significant.

00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:36.956
Because Pence is arguing

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:38.024
that he should be protected

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:39.025
from this subpoena

00:02:39.025 --> 00:02:40.059
under the Constitution

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:41.761
speech or debate clause.

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:42.962
Now that clauses supposed

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:44.164
to protect legislators

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:46.266
from any sort of law enforcement activity

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:47.433
that covers

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:49.802
their actual work in Congress,

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:51.037
Pence argues

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:52.205
that as president of the Senate,

00:02:52.205 --> 00:02:53.373
he should qualify.

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:55.175
But this judge in the op ed he's

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:56.509
very clear about how he feels.

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:57.243
He says, look, Jack

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:58.678
Smith's subpoena was neither

00:02:58.678 --> 00:02:59.646
politically motivated

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:01.214
nor designed to strengthen President

00:03:01.214 --> 00:03:03.349
Biden's political hand in 2024.

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:05.018
Thus, the jarring dissonance

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:06.286
between the subpoena and Mr.

00:03:06.286 --> 00:03:08.321
Pence's characterization of it.

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:08.788
It is Mr.

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:10.790
Pence who has chosen to politicize

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:13.059
the subpoena, not the DOJ.

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:15.094
But I will also point out

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:15.728
that The Wall Street

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:18.031
Journal editorial board recently came out

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:19.732
and had a completely different take.

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:20.867
They argued that

00:03:20.867 --> 00:03:23.203
because of what Pence did on January 6th,

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:23.770
he should be given

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:25.171
the benefit of the doubt.

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:26.406
So clearly,

00:03:26.406 --> 00:03:27.207
intelligent minds

00:03:27.207 --> 00:03:27.674
can disagree

00:03:27.674 --> 00:03:28.708
about the Pence subpoena,

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:29.943
but the opinions that really matter

00:03:29.943 --> 00:03:30.944
will come from the courts.

00:03:30.944 --> 00:03:31.911
And this issue

00:03:31.911 --> 00:03:32.612
could go all the way

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:33.580
to the Supreme Court.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:34.681
And he's like a treasure map

00:03:34.681 --> 00:03:36.516
to like some sort of something.

00:03:36.516 --> 00:03:37.884
Tell me about it.

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:38.351
I know

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:40.153
Paul is like you telling me,

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:41.888
Paul has won an office.

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:43.356
Paul Ryan, great reporting.

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:44.724
And thank you for explaining all of them.

00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:46.092
Bring it all down. Thank you so much.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:48.828
I promised.

00:03:48.828 --> 00:03:49.862
That is House Speaker

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:50.663
Kevin McCarthy's

00:03:50.663 --> 00:03:53.566
defense for sharing 40000 hours

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:54.400
of security footage

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:55.668
from the Capitol insurrection

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:57.737
with Fox News host Tucker Carlson

00:03:57.737 --> 00:03:58.371
and the past.

00:03:58.371 --> 00:03:59.038
McCarthy said

00:03:59.038 --> 00:03:59.672
Donald Trump

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:02.709
was responsible for the attack.

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:04.877
The president bears responsibility

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:05.678
for Wednesday's

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:07.847
attack on Congress by mob rioters.

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:09.749
He should have immediately

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:11.050
denounced the mob

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:13.453
when he saw what was unfolding.

00:04:13.453 --> 00:04:15.722
These facts require immediate action

00:04:16.022 --> 00:04:17.624
by President Trump.

00:04:17.624 --> 00:04:18.825
But now McCarthy tells The New York

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:19.592
Times, quote,

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:20.326
I was asked in

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:21.594
the press about these tapes

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:22.095
and I said,

00:04:22.095 --> 00:04:23.763
they do belong to the American public.

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:25.665
I think Sunshine lets

00:04:25.665 --> 00:04:27.467
everybody make their own judgment.

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:28.735
Democrats have been condemning

00:04:28.735 --> 00:04:30.370
McCarthy for the move, warning

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:31.938
that it creates a significant security

00:04:31.938 --> 00:04:32.238
risk.

00:04:32.238 --> 00:04:33.139
Here's what Congressman

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:34.207
Democratic Congressman Jamie

00:04:34.207 --> 00:04:35.241
Raskin said last night.

00:04:37.243 --> 00:04:39.078
We have security concerns

00:04:39.078 --> 00:04:40.546
about turning over

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:42.749
the location of security cameras

00:04:42.749 --> 00:04:44.817
in the US Capitol that the police use.

00:04:44.984 --> 00:04:47.053
We have concern about the escape

00:04:47.086 --> 00:04:48.354
and evacuation routes

00:04:48.354 --> 00:04:49.689
that were used on that day.

00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:52.258
We don't want to just,

00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:52.592
you know,

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:53.793
throw our hands up and say, well, let's

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:55.361
just let everything go

00:04:55.361 --> 00:04:56.929
and let the insurrectionists

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:58.731
have the materials that will allow them

00:04:58.731 --> 00:05:00.900
to plan the next January 6th.

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:02.735
In a letter to Senate colleagues

00:05:02.735 --> 00:05:04.037
Wednesday, Majority Leader

00:05:04.037 --> 00:05:04.671
Chuck Schumer

00:05:04.671 --> 00:05:06.572
said McCarthy's actions, quote, laid bare

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:07.740
that this sham is simply

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:08.641
about pandering

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:10.777
to MAGA election deniers, not the truth.

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:12.612
Well, it is true

00:05:12.612 --> 00:05:13.746
that his most conservative

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:15.181
members wanted him to release this.

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:16.582
They've been pushing him to do it.

00:05:16.582 --> 00:05:17.684
That's why he's doing it.

00:05:17.684 --> 00:05:19.352
But I think the risk that you hear from

00:05:19.352 --> 00:05:20.553
other Republicans is they

00:05:20.553 --> 00:05:22.088
do not want to talk about January six,

00:05:22.088 --> 00:05:23.456
and this is just relitigating it.

00:05:23.456 --> 00:05:24.691
And they don't think that works

00:05:24.691 --> 00:05:25.925
in their favor.

00:05:25.925 --> 00:05:26.759
And then releasing it,

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:28.828
I mean, quite honestly, to

00:05:28.828 --> 00:05:29.429
a person

00:05:29.429 --> 00:05:31.764
in the media who the courts have deemed

00:05:32.699 --> 00:05:34.500
not legitimate news for that,

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.069
it is basically editorial

00:05:36.069 --> 00:05:38.838
And so it's not a news program.

00:05:38.838 --> 00:05:39.806
I don't know what people

00:05:39.806 --> 00:05:40.807
I can't say

00:05:40.807 --> 00:05:41.874
whether it should have been released

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:43.843
or not, not have been released.

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:45.845
But I think if it is, he should release

00:05:45.845 --> 00:05:46.379
all the news

00:05:46.379 --> 00:05:47.814
organizations in sunshine,

00:05:47.814 --> 00:05:49.482
something that shines on everyone.

00:05:49.482 --> 00:05:51.150
One, right.

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:52.585
Much as they do with the foyer request,

00:05:52.585 --> 00:05:54.387
when people have a four year request

00:05:54.387 --> 00:05:56.222
to CNN, does it for your request?

00:05:56.222 --> 00:05:58.458
Everybody gets the information right.

00:05:58.725 --> 00:06:00.626
If Kevin McCarthy

00:06:00.626 --> 00:06:01.728
wants to release it to the media,

00:06:01.728 --> 00:06:03.363
then you release it to everybody

00:06:03.363 --> 00:06:04.330
so that everybody can get

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:05.198
a bite at the Apple

00:06:05.198 --> 00:06:07.266
and there can be, as as he says,

00:06:07.266 --> 00:06:08.534
a punchline. Yeah.

